acklog claim.\n\nFixtures: all 20 definition files match manifest.json sha256 and are blob-identical to the named public commits; no telemetry, paths, ids or names beyond the manifest digests. Everything runs in t.TempDir() except a system temp directory for the unix socket path, removed after each cycle; no live home, socket, database, launchd or install is touched.\n\nBinary reproducibility: I rebuilt with the recorded build command and environment (-trimpath, the stampedSourceURL ldflag, GOFLAGS empty, GOPROXY off, CGO on, go1.27.0 darwin/arm64) and obtained SHA256 fcb54bb4476a1be4a4f14eefb89f6b74616cd7d54109310894389a64381461ae, matching the attached binary-result.json and the requester's three retained builds. The attached input manifest records 1,974 inputs over 405 packages with one changed from the accepted reference; the omission-result attachment records the expected failure when e.position is restored. That evidence lives in the primary artifact's attachments, not in the head, and this review vouches for what I reproduced: the head builds deterministically to the published hash. The bridge from that hash to the installed dirty binary remains the previously accepted qualified reference (3922/3923), as the evidence itself states.\n\nDestination: request 3925 carries target_ref refs/heads/recovery/resident-5d84-pending, target_head 5d84ac71 and this workroom as target_repo; that branch is at exact 5d84ac71 locally and on origin. The attached actual-non-main-succession result shows publish 25, retire 25, left_live 2 with current-main publication 3906 (dc18025b) preserved despite its abandoned label, per Hugh; I did not run merge-plan because the state@3 tool requires a ratified approval, so that check follows ratification as the request says. This approval does not authorize retiring 3906 or any classifier change.\n\nArchitecture: inbox layer only; resident, control, definition and projection layers are untouched in production code and their contracts are exercised unchanged by the fixture. No runtime, schema, authority or data-format change.\n\nSecurity: dependency and toolchain manifest unchanged and verified; historical definition identities asserted, not rewritten; synthetic fixture custody confirmed; no live operations; queries bounded by the existing limit; failure and restart conservation exercised. No unresolved security defect.\n\nSimplification: the production change is four lines net. The test machinery is proportionate; the manifest's commit field is used only by reviewers and the legacy cost is logged rather than asserted, which is the right choice for a CPU-independent gate. Nothing to cut.\n\nNo installation, service replacement, intake, launchd, live database or schema action is authorized by this verdict.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:a790a35d5830016dbc95c1ab6aab115f24626228","head":"f36cb0eb2645cce40ebd30466406d0f293e6b455","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:e387ee922b547dc32d209f84416f1c8008a81e11\",\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:23eff22934e444c47f12f50ce403fa26339d962e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:23eff22934e444c47f12f50ce403fa26339d962e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}